## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design practical multilingual quality checks that balance latency, privacy, and real-world data issues. It also probes how candidates combine simple heuristics with a small model and how they plan evaluation and rollout.

## Key Concepts
- Multilingual NLP basics and translation quality signals
- Hybrid rule-based plus lightweight ML approaches
- Privacy-preserving inference and latency budgeting
- Offline annotation plans and staged canary rollout

## Code Example
```javascript
function simpleMistranslationFlag(src, trans){
  // naive cue: detect presence/absence of 'not' showing sentiment flip
  const sSrc = /not|n't/.test(src) ? -1 : 1;
  const sTrans = /not|n't/.test(trans) ? -1 : 1;
  return Math.abs(sSrc - sTrans) > 0;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you scale to 10+ languages with minimal drift?
- What metrics and alarms would you attach to the canary rollout?

## Why This Question Is Asked

This question assesses the ability to design real-time, multilingual NLP systems that balance privacy, governance, latency constraints, and safe escalation.

## Key Concepts

- Real-time streaming NLP with strict latency budgets
- Privacy-by-design with on-device preprocessing
- Multilingual toxic text detection and debiasing
- Drift detection and governance hooks for human escalation
- Operational readiness: rollout, monitoring, and rollback strategies

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudocode: redaction + toxicity routing
function processMessage(msg) {
  // Stage 1: PII redaction
  const redacted = redactPII(msg.text);

  // Stage 2: Toxicity classification
  const prediction = await classifier.predict(redacted);

  // Stage 3: Policy gate routing
  if (prediction.score > HIGH_RISK_THRESHOLD) {
    queueForHumanReview({ ...msg, redactedText: redacted, prediction });
  } else {
    publishMessage({ ...msg, redactedText: redacted, prediction });
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical detection of AI-generated content with model attribution, latency constraints, multilingual support, and robust auditing in a live chat setting.

## Key Concepts
- Real-time on-device + cloud inference
- AI-generated content detection and model attribution
- Per-post explainability and tamper-evident auditing
- Drift detection and privacy-preserving processing

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo on-device scorer and cloud orchestrator
function scorePost(post) {
  const local = localModel.predict(post.text);
  if (local.confidence > 0.6) return {flag: true, score: local.confidence, method:'local'};
  // fallback to cloud for deeper check
  return CloudService.analyze(post).then(r => ({flag: r.flag, score: r.score, method:'cloud'}));
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle multilingual coverage and language drift over time?
- What metrics and rollback plan would you use for production calibration and user impact assessment?

